<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    CineVault network security policy.

    D16-R2-DEVICE1:
    CineVault-to-CineVault Nearby Sharing intentionally uses an ephemeral
    HTTP endpoint on the local LAN. Android 9+ blocks cleartext HTTP unless
    the app explicitly opts in, which allowed discovery to succeed but
    blocked the first pairing request on physical devices.

    Android Network Security Config cannot express a dynamic RFC1918/local-LAN
    allow-list that covers arbitrary home/hotel/router subnets. Nearby hosts
    are discovered at runtime and may use 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, or
    other locally routed addresses. Cleartext is therefore permitted at the
    Android HTTP-stack level so the runtime CineVault networking layer can
    reach discovered LAN peers.

    This does NOT put credentials in URLs or discovery records. CineVault
    Nearby still uses its pairing/approval/session-token policy, and Vault /
    Restricted content remains excluded by the sharing policy.

    SMB is unaffected by this file because jcifs-ng uses its own socket
    transport rather than Android's HTTP stack.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
